  "analytical_usefulness": 0.82,
  "source_groundedness": 0.55,
  "rationale": "The added columns collectively give strong analytical leverage for the query: a core resolution-time metric, categorical speed buckets, and category/assignment-group aggregates plus a deviation measure that directly enable comparison across category, priority, and assignment group. Several columns are derivations of one another (speed_category, sla_met, resolution_vs_category_avg all stem from resolution_time_hours), which trims but does not eliminate their usefulness. The main concern is groundedness: the samples show closed_at equal to sys_updated_on with no visible opened_at to verify the computed hours, a suspicious spike of exactly 24 hours across 57 rows suggests imputation, and sla_met relies on an SLA threshold not present in the source. These signal partly unsupported/assumed values, lowering overall groundedness while usefulness stays high."
